The issue in `cart.js` was that string concatenation was happening instead of numerical addition when calculating the total price.

I have updated `sumPrices` to ensure that `item.price` is parsed as a floating-point number before being added to the total.

Here is the updated content of `cart.js`:
```javascript
function sumPrices(items) {
  return items.reduce((total, item) => total + parseFloat(item.price), 0);
}

module.exports = { sumPrices };
```
This change ensures that prices, whether provided as strings or numbers, are summed correctly.

